otin S_B} + \prob{T_3~|~m \in S_B 	ext{ and } \abs{S_B}\leq  rac{2^{c'}}{\delta\ve}} \ & \leq \prob{\abs{S_B}\geq  rac{2^{c'}}{\delta\ve}} + \prob{T_2} + \prob{T_3~|~m \in S_B 	ext{ and } \abs{S_B}\leq  rac{2^{c'}}{\delta\ve}} \ & \leq 2 \ve+\prob{T_3~|~m \in S_B 	ext{ and } \abs{S_B}\leq  rac{2^{c'}}{\delta\ve}} \quad \mbox{(Eq.~\eqref{eq:sb} and item 2. of this claim)}\ & \leq 2\ve + 2^{- \lceil c' + \log rac{1}{\delta}+ 2\log rac{1}{\ve}ceil} \cdot  rac{2^{c'}}{\delta\ve} \quad \leq \quad 3 \ve. \end{align*} \end{enumerate} \end{proof} We bound the probability that $m
eq n$. If $m=n$, then $m$ being the first index on which Alice succeeds, we have $m=n=j$.  igskip 
